Received arguments:
{
  "case_state": "Ticket NBL-040-tenant-resolved is at the landlord gate. Event 008: tenant Rowan says the washing machine is fixed by swapping in their own machine, and the faulty one is in the garage. Event 009: landlord Oliver agreed to someone checking the machine, sent 12:12 UTC, after the tenant's 11:47 message. The landlord may not know about the swap. No provider assigned, no visit booked, no landlord decision recorded. The job is on hold for the landlord until 2026-12-28.</case_state>\n<parameter name=\"next_actions\">[{\"action\":\"Ask the landlord whether the check visit is still wanted now that the tenant has swapped the machine, and whether the tenant's own machine can stay installed.\",\"recipient\":\"Oliver, landlord\",\"channel\":\"email\",\"ledger_id\":\"A1\"},{\"action\":\"Tell the tenant the landlord has been asked, no visit is booked, and to keep the old machine stored safely and report any leak or fault.\",\"recipient\":\"Rowan, tenant\",\"channel\":\"email\",\"ledger_id\":\"A2\"},{\"action\":\"Hold the job for the landlord's reply with a review date of 2026-12-28.\",\"recipient\":\"internal\",\"channel\":\"internal\",\"ledger_id\":\"A4\"}]",
  "boundaries": [
    "The tenant's claim that the fault is fixed is not verified. No engineer has looked at either machine.",
    "Sending the messages does not mean the landlord has agreed to anything. No landlord decision is recorded.",
    "The tenant's own machine being installed is not yet approved by the landlord.",
    "No provider was assigned and no visit was booked. No spend was approved.",
    "The landlord's agreement to a check is not recorded as a decision, because the swap may have changed what is needed.",
    "The ticket was not closed. Closing needs a landlord reply and a completed work result."
  ],
  "remaining_work": [
    "Landlord (Oliver) to say whether the check visit is still wanted and whether the tenant's machine can stay. Owner: operations, review 2026-12-28.",
    "If the check is wanted, record the landlord decision, assign a provider and book the visit.",
    "If the landlord says no, record the outcome, tell the tenant and landlord, and close without payment.",
    "Confirm the ticket reference: the messages were logged against NBL-040-4451 but the ticket is NBL-040-tenant-resolved. Check the message log."
  ],
  "missing_info": [
    "Whether the landlord still wants a check after the tenant's swap.",
    "Whether the landlord agrees to the tenant's own washing machine staying in the flat.",
    "Independent confirmation that the washing machine works (no work result yet).",
    "Which machine is landlord-owned and which is the tenant's."
  ],
  "outcome": "action_taken",
  "severity": "routine",
  "summary": "The tenant says they fixed the washing machine by swapping in their own, but the landlord agreed to a check at 12:12 UTC, possibly without knowing about the swap. I asked the landlord whether the check is still needed and whether the tenant's machine can stay, and told the tenant no visit is booked yet. The job is on hold for the landlord until 2026-12-28.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "question": "Where does this case stand right now, and what is outstanding?",
      "answer": "The job is at the landlord gate and on hold. The landlord agreed to a check, but the tenant reports the fault is fixed by a swap. The landlord has not been asked about the swap yet, and the tenant's machine has not been approved. Outstanding: the landlord's decision on whether the check is still needed and whether the tenant's machine can stay."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the next action, who is it for, and through which channel?",
      "answer": "Email the landlord Oliver to ask whether the check is still wanted and whether the tenant's machine can stay (ledger A1). Email the tenant Rowan to say the landlord has been asked and no visit is booked, and to keep the old machine safe (ledger A2). Hold the job for the landlord until 2026-12-28 (ledger A4)."
    },
    {
      "question": "Does anything need a human decision, and why?",
      "answer": "Not yet. The landlord's answer decides whether a provider visit is needed or the job can close, and that is a routine landlord decision. No escalation is needed unless the landlord's reply conflicts with the tenant's account or the appliance installation raises a safety concern."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "description": "Email to landlord Oliver asking whether the check is still wanted after the tenant's swap, and whether the tenant's machine can stay."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Email to tenant Rowan saying the landlord has been asked, no visit is booked, and to keep the old machine safely stored."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A4",
      "description": "Job NBL-040-tenant-resolved put on hold for the landlord with review date 2026-12-28."
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "handling": "put_on_hold on NBL-040-4451 failed (ticket not found). Used list_tickets to find the correct ref NBL-040-tenant-resolved and re-applied the hold (A4), verified."
    }
  ],
  "conflicts": [
    "Tenant (event 008) says the washing machine is fixed by swapping machines; landlord (event 009) agreed to a check of the washing machine. Trusted the tenant's latest report for the facts but did not treat it as verified, and asked the landlord before acting.",
    "The ticket reference in the case text is NBL-040-4451, which is the provider's reference. The system ticket is NBL-040-tenant-resolved. The two messages were sent with the first reference in their ticket field, so the message log may need tidying."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The landlord's reply at event 009 was written before they knew about the tenant's swap.",
    "The tenant's email at event 008 is accurate about the swap."
  ]
}

